{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Summable","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Field"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_phiBProd_le_of_den_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_phiBProd_le_of_den_lower","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdStripBound.lean#L145-L154","doc":"**G3 (phiBProd strip bound).** Given a denominator **lower** bound `δ > 0` (the G2\nobligation), the ratio `phiBProd = num/den` is bounded on the strip by\n`exp(∑' ‖numFactorₖ − 1‖)/δ`. Off the `b`-zero-lattice for the numerator; the `δ`\nhypothesis carries the denominator's non-vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_tprod_denFactor_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_tprod_denFactor_le","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdStripBound.lean#L135-L143","doc":"**G1 (denominator upper bound).** Off the dual lattice (all `denFactor` nonzero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_tprod_numFactor_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_tprod_numFactor_le","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdStripBound.lean#L124-L133","doc":"**G1 (numerator upper bound).** Off the `b`-zero-lattice (all `numFactor` nonzero), the\nnumerator product is bounded by `exp` of the summed factor-log-norms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_tprod_one_add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdStripBound.norm_tprod_one_add_le","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdStripBound.lean#L38-L57","doc":"**General product-norm upper bound.** For a norm-summable complex family `g` with no\nvanishing factor `1 + gₖ`, `‖∏' k, (1 + gₖ)‖ ≤ exp(∑' k, ‖gₖ‖)`. Proof: `‖∏‖ = ∏‖·‖`\n(`Multipliable.norm_tprod`); with all factors positive, `∏‖1+gₖ‖ = exp(∑ log‖1+gₖ‖)`\n(`rexp_tsum_eq_tprod`); and `log‖1+gₖ‖ ≤ ‖1+gₖ‖ − 1 ≤ ‖gₖ‖`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}